cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or these findings, please cite it as below."
title: "unused-assumptions: theorems in Mathlib whose stated setting exceeds what their proof requires"
abstract: >-
  A mechanical search over Mathlib for theorems whose stated algebraic setting is
  stronger than their own proof needs: replace one instance binder with a weaker
  class, keep the proof unchanged, compile it alone. Published with the data and
  a verifier that recompiles every row.
authors:
  - family-names: Perassi
    given-names: Carlo
type: dataset
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/carlok/unused-assumptions"
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formalised mathematics
  - typeclass generalisation
